    "ceiling_height_rule": {
      "group": "interior",
      "binding": "specified",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "judgment": true,
      "rule": "Ceiling height is not derived by a harmonic mean of the room's own plan proportion. Nothing here is composed as a whole; the governing dimensions are the corredor bay (3-4 m) and the viga span fixing range depth (5-6 m), not a proportioned ceiling height.",
      "note": "OVERRIDES a cascade fill from renaissance-classical (a harmonic-mean-of-plan-proportion rule). This contradicts the node's own bound room-role pack: this style's own proportion_packs binds `room-vernacular` (precedence 1), and its own governing_logic states in as many words that 'nothing is derived from an order, and no elevation is composed as a whole -- the composition is a plan.' Confirmed with `resolve_kit.py mexican-hacienda --slot ceiling_height_rule --verbose`, whose PACK RESOLUTION shows room-vernacular, not room-harmonic, as the pack that actually governs this slot by precedence. Fixed here per WP-4.2 instructions; the identical fix is made on mexican-colonial.kit.json for the same reason."
    },
